   shows: an artifact type label (e.g. "Training data"), the hosting
   platform (e.g. "Zenodo"), and a direct off-site link.

   The card reads as browsable supplementary material, not a primary call
   to action: no primary-button chrome, no Open Blue fills. It belongs
   alongside abstract metadata, not competing with the PDF / HTML buttons.

   COLUMN LAYOUT  Three-column CSS grid on each row link:
     - Type   (2fr): artifact category label — bold, Repository Brown
     - Platform (1fr): hosting service name — muted, Library Grey
     - URL    (3fr): the link text with off-site icon — Link Blue

   OFF-SITE SIGNAL  Every row navigates off-site. Three independent cues:
     1. target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" on every row link
     2. A visible ↗ icon (stroke SVG, aria-hidden="true")
     3. Screen-reader text "(opens in new tab)" via .is-sr-only
   This satisfies WCAG 1.4.1 — color is not the sole signal.

   OVERFLOW  1–5 rows: always visible. 6 or more rows: the first 5 rows
   are visible; rows 6+ receive the HTML `hidden` attribute injected by
   JavaScript; a .ds-artifact-show-all disclosure button (also JS-
   injected) reveals them all on click. Without JavaScript, every row
   remains visible — scripts must never carry content
   (DESIGN-POLICIES.md, progressive enhancement).

   The count threshold and the disclosure button text are chosen per the
   "Truncation always signals continuation" preference order in
   DESIGN-POLICIES.md: (1) disclosure with explicit count over
   (2) internal scrolling. The button label must always state the total
   (e.g. "Show all 12 links") so the count is visible before expansion.

   HOVER + FOCUS  The entire row is an interactive block link
   (.ds-artifact-row-link, display: grid) so mouse users can click
   anywhere on the row; Tab stops at each <a>. Hover: Card Grey fill
   on the link element. Focus: :focus-visible ring with outline-offset
   -2px so the ring sits inside the card rather than bleeding outside.
   Row height: 10px vertical padding + 14px type × 1.4 leading ≈ 40px
   — well above the 24px WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 target-size floor.

   RESPONSIVE  ≤520px: the three-column grid switches to a flex-wrap
   layout — artifact type on its own line, platform + URL on the second.

   Validated: 2026-07-28 (initial promotion to design-system.css).
   Reference: design-patterns/public/artifact-links-styles.html.

   Example:
     <section class="ds-artifact-card" aria-labelledby="artifacts-hd">
       <h2 class="ds-artifact-card-heading" id="artifacts-hd">
         Datasets &amp; code
       </h2>
       <ul class="ds-artifact-list" role="list">
         <li class="ds-artifact-row">
           <a class="ds-artifact-row-link"
              href="https://zenodo.org/record/8231451"
              target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
             <span class="ds-artifact-type">Training data</span>
             <span class="ds-artifact-platform">Zenodo</span>
             <span class="ds-artifact-url-cell">
               zenodo.org/record/8231451
               <svg class="ds-artifact-ext-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                    fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
                    stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
                    aria-hidden="true">
                 <path d="M7 17L17 7"/><path d="M7 7h10v10"/>
               </svg>
